  "description": "QIQZEZ crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C50 H108 N14 Nd8 O48 2+,2(C2 H3 N1),2(N1 O3 1-). From the CIF bond table, Nd1 (Nd) has 8 O neighbors; Nd2 (Nd) has 8 O neighbors; Nd3 (Nd) has 8 O neighbors; Nd4 (Nd) has 8 O neighbors; Nd1D (Nd) has 8 O neighbors; Nd2D (Nd) has 8 O neighbors; Nd3D (Nd) has 8 O neighbors; Nd4D (Nd) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 13 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.777-5.599 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 88.60-177.48°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Nd8(H2L)4(HL)4(NO3)6(CO3)2](NO3)2·2CH3CN. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 6 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 6 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
